const SPAWNPROOF = /glass|slab$|stairs$|carpet|leaves|_wall$|fence|pane$|barrier|hopper|trapdoor|ice$|bedrock|magma|_bars$/;
const k = (p) => p.join(",");

/**
 * A row (or a back-to-back pair of rows) of sockets. units: "DS DS" / ["deep","shallow",...] / a number of tenant
 * units (each a deep and a shallow socket, 8 of frontage). rows: 2 adds the facing row across a service aisle, deep
 * against shallow (spec rule 7): it shifts by a bay so each deep socket backs onto a shallow one.
 */
export function layoutSockets({ face = "south", at = [0, 5, 0], floorY, units = 1, rows = 1, aisle = 2, backWall = true } = {}) {
  const y0 = floorY ?? at[1], base = [at[0], y0, at[2]];
  const kinds = typeof units === "number" ? Array.from({ length: units }, () => UNIT).flat()
    : (Array.isArray(units) ? units : String(units).replace(/\s+/g, "").split("")).map((c) => ({ D: "deep", S: "shallow", d: "deep", s: "shallow" })[c] ?? c);
  if (kinds.some((t) => !KINDS[t])) throw new Error(`sockets: units are deep (D) or shallow (S), got ${kinds.join(",")}`);
  const OPPOSITE = { north: "south", south: "north", east: "west", west: "east" };
  const sockets = [], wallLines = [];
  const rowOf = (F, kindsRow, row) => {
    kindsRow.forEach((kind, i) => {
      const K = KINDS[kind], u0 = i * BAY + 1, cells = (fn) => { const out = []; fn(out); return out; };
      const p = (u, v, d) => F.p(u0 + u, v - 0, d);
      const box = cells((o) => { for (let u = 0; u < 3; u++) for (let v = BOTTOM; v <= K.top; v++) for (let d = 0; d > -K.depth; d--) o.push(p(u, v, d)); });
      sockets.push({
        id: `${row ? "B" : "A"}${i + 1}`, row, kind, takes: K.takes, face: F.face, lanes: [0, 1, 2].map((u) => p(u, 0, 0)),
        box: { from: p(0, BOTTOM, -(K.depth - 1)), to: p(2, K.top, 0) },
        hoppers: K.hoppers.map((u) => p(u, 0, -3)),                                  // rule 3: 3 back, top flush at y 0
        counter: K.hoppers.flatMap((u) => [p(u, 0, 0), p(u, 0, -1)]),               // the 2 solid cells in front of it
        openFront: cells((o) => { for (let u = 0; u < 3; u++) for (let v = 1; v <= 3; v++) for (let d = 0; d >= -2; d--) o.push(p(u, v, d)); }),  // rule 4
        backWall: backWall ? cells((o) => { for (let u = 0; u < 3; u++) for (let v = BOTTOM; v <= K.top; v++) o.push(p(u, v, -K.depth)); }) : [],
        pit: cells((o) => { for (let u = 0; u < 3; u++) for (let d = 0; d > -K.depth; d--) o.push(p(u, BOTTOM - 1, d)); }),      // under the machine's floor
        ceiling: cells((o) => { for (let u = 0; u < 3; u++) for (let d = 0; d > -K.depth; d--) for (let v = K.top + 1; v < FLOOR_ABOVE; v++) o.push(p(u, v, d)); }),  // rule 2
        fascia: cells((o) => { for (let u = 0; u < 3; u++) for (let v = 4; v <= K.top; v++) o.push(p(u, v, 1)); }),  // closes the header from the street
        front: cells((o) => { for (let u = -1; u <= 3; u++) for (let v = 1; v <= 3; v++) for (let d = 1; d <= 2; d++) o.push(p(u, v, d)); }),  // 2 in front, y 1-3
        service: cells((o) => { for (let u = 0; u < 3; u++) o.push(p(u, 0, -K.depth - 1)); }),                    // the aisle behind the back wall
      });
    });
    for (let i = 0; i <= kindsRow.length; i++) {
      const left = kindsRow[i - 1], right = kindsRow[i], depth = Math.max(KINDS[left]?.depth ?? 0, KINDS[right]?.depth ?? 0), top = Math.max(KINDS[left]?.top ?? 0, KINDS[right]?.top ?? 0);
      const line = [];
      for (let v = BOTTOM; v <= top; v++) for (let d = 0; d > -depth; d--) line.push(F.p(i * BAY, v, d));
      wallLines.push({ row: F.face, u: i * BAY, cells: line });
    }
  };
